{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatSubword"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.subword_property_of_leftReflLe_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.subword_property_of_leftReflLe_An","kind":"theorem","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L391-L396","doc":"The subword corollary in left-handed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_leftReflLe_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_leftReflLe_An","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L380-L389","doc":"**`LeftReflLe → BruhatLe` in type `A`, hypothesis-free** — the left-handed mirror of\n`bruhatLe_of_reflLe_An`, and the lemma a Mathas Prop. 3.7 consumer actually needs.\n\nProof: transport to the right-handed statement through `⁻¹`, apply\n`bruhatLe_of_reflLe_An`, transport the conclusion back with\n`CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_inv_iff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflLe_inv_of_leftReflLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflLe_inv_of_leftReflLe","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L372-L378","doc":"The chain version of `reflStep_inv_of_leftReflStep`.  Note the chain does **not** reverse:\n`⁻¹` is applied pointwise, and `ReflTransGen` is closed under that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflStep_inv_of_leftReflStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflStep_inv_of_leftReflStep","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L363-L370","doc":"A left step inverts to a right step: `t⁻¹ = t` for a reflection, and `ℓ` is\ninversion-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.LeftReflLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.LeftReflLe","kind":"def","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L360-L361","doc":"**The left-handed reflection-generated order.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.LeftReflStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.LeftReflStep","kind":"def","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L354-L358","doc":"One upward step **on the left**: `w = t · v` for a reflection `t`, with the length going up.\n\nThe mirror of `ReflStep`.  It exists because the tableau side of Mathas' Prop. 3.7 produces\nleft multiplications (`TableauPerm.dOf_smul`), while `ReflStep` is right-handed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.subword_property_of_reflLe_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.subword_property_of_reflLe_An","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L341-L347","doc":"**What this buys a Mathas consumer, spelled out.** Given `u ⊵ v ⊵ w` in the reflection sense on\na type-`A` system, `u` appears as a subword of *every* reduced word for `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_reflLe_An","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_reflLe_An","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L336-L339","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflStep_mul_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflStep_mul_simple","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L308-L332","doc":"**Upward lifting, one step.** If `y = x·t` is a single upward reflection step and `s` is a right\n*ascent* of both `x` and `y`, then `x·s → y·s` is a single upward reflection step too — the\nreflection being the conjugate `s t s`.\n\nThis is the piece the converse bridge needs iterated, and it is stated here so that the header's\nclaim about it is a theorem rather than an assertion. **What does not follow is the chain version**:\na `ReflLe` is a `ReflTransGen`, nothing forces `s` to remain an ascent at the intermediate elements,\nand `ReflStep` is not defined for a descent. That gap is the open problem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.not_forall_bruhatLe_of_sublist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.not_forall_bruhatLe_of_sublist","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L284-L304","doc":"**The non-reduced-subword statement is FALSE.**\n\nAn earlier note in this file proposed closing `BruhatLe → ReflLe` via *\"a subword of an arbitrary\n(not necessarily reduced) word for `w` still gives `u ≤ w`\"*. It does not hold, and this is the\none-line reason: `π [i, i] = 1` while `π [i] = sᵢ`, and `[i]` is a subword of `[i, i]`.\n\nRecorded as a theorem rather than as prose because it is a plausible thing to reach for and the\nprose form of it stood in this file for one commit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.lifting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.lifting","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L258-L280","doc":"**Lifting, part two — the property proper.** If `s` is a right descent of *both* `u` and `w`,\nand `u ≤ w`, then `u·s ≤ w·s`.\n\nThe branch where the subword used the final `s` gives it outright. The other branch gives `u ≤ w·s`,\nand `u·s ≤ u` because `s` is a descent of `u` — a single reflection step — so transitivity finishes\nit. This is the fourth of the four properties `QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat` deferred. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_mul_simple_of_isRightDescent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_mul_simple_of_isRightDescent","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L240-L256","doc":"**Lifting, part one.** If `s` is a right descent of `w` and `u ≤ w`, then `u·s ≤ w`.\n\nNo induction: the subword property hands over a subword of a reduced word for `w` ending in `s`,\nand *either* branch of the split already exhibits `u·s`. If the subword used the final `s`, drop it;\nif it did not, append it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.exists_reduced_concat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.exists_reduced_concat","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L210-L229","doc":"A right descent is witnessed by a reduced word ending in that letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflStep_of_eraseIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflStep_of_eraseIdx","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L178-L206","doc":"**Deleting one letter of a reduced word is a downward reflection step.**\n\nThe reflection is the `j`-th entry of Mathlib's right inversion sequence, and\n`wordProd_mul_getD_rightInvSeq` is the identity that names it. This is the atom the converse\ndirection would iterate.\n\n🛑 **Iterating it does not give `BruhatLe → ReflLe`.** A subword deletes several letters, the\nintermediate words are not reduced, and `ReflStep` demands a *strict length increase* at every step\n— which the intermediate products need not provide. The converse is proved in\n`QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatConverse`, and **not** by iterating this: it peels a right descent instead\nand lifts. This lemma is not the route; it is kept because it is the honest atom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_reflLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_reflLe","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L163-L174","doc":"**`ReflLe → BruhatLe`.** Mathas' Bruhat order refines into this corpus's subword one, so every\nstatement proved about `BruhatLe` — the subword property, transitivity, antisymmetry — is available\nto a consumer whose hypothesis is stated in the reflection form.\n\nUsed to carry `DihedralExact` / `M i j ≠ 0` because it chains with `bruhatLe_trans`; both are now\nproved in `CoxeterDihedralOrder`, so it is unconditional. The one-step\nlemma above needs neither. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_reflStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.bruhatLe_of_reflStep","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L145-L159","doc":"**A single upward reflection step lands inside the subword order.**\n\n`t` is a right inversion of `w = v · t`, so `strong_exchange` produces a *single deleted letter* of\nany reduced word for `w` whose product is `v`. Nothing here needs Matsumoto. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflLe_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflLe_trans","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L140-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflLe_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.reflLe_refl","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L138-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.ReflLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.ReflLe","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L134-L136","doc":"**The reflection-generated Bruhat order** — Mathas' `⊵`. Transitive and reflexive by\nconstruction, being a reflexive–transitive closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.ReflStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BruhatReflection.ReflStep","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BruhatReflection.lean#L131-L132","doc":"One upward step: `w = v · t` for a reflection `t`, with the length going up. ","signatureChunk":0}]}